{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS7cfF1DmPncbQ6BsjG1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The first publish works only because the table is empty. Every publish after that saves a float similarity score, and DynamoDB's Python library (boto3) rejects floats.\n\n**Cause:** Each story is saved with its most similar existing stories and a `score` for each. `similarity()` returned that score as a Python float, so `put_item` raised `TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.` and the handler turned that into a 500. On the first publish there are no other stories, so the list is empty (`similar=0` in the log) and there's no float to reject. The old test only published one story, so it never hit this.\n\n**Fix, in `src/app.py`:**\n- **The score itself:** `similarity()` now returns a `Decimal` built from the rounded value.\n- **Keeping it from coming back:** a new `to_dynamo()` function converts every float in the item to `Decimal`, and `publish()` runs it right before `put_item`. A float field added later will be converted instead of breaking publishing.\n- **Related problem:** `tags` that aren't a list of strings (e.g. `[1.5]`) caused a 500. They now get a 400.\n\n**Tests:** I added 4 regression tests, including publishing several related stories in a row. All 4 fail on the original code with the same error as production, and all 5 tests pass with the fix.\n\nOne thing I didn't change: `table.scan()` isn't paginated, so it only reads the first 1 MB of the table. Once the library grows, \"similar\" stories will come from only part of it.\n\nThe cause and fix are written up in `ANSWER.md`. Nothing was committed or deployed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":983,"cache_read_input_tokens":26975,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":983},"outp