es instead.` and the handler turned that into a 500. On the first publish there are no other stories, so the list is empty (`similar=0` in the log) and there's no float to reject. The old test only published one story, so it never hit this.\n\n**Fix, in `src/app.py`:**\n- **The score itself:** `similarity()` now returns a `Decimal` built from the rounded value.\n- **Keeping it from coming back:** a new `to_dynamo()` function converts every float in the item to `Decimal`, and `publish()` runs it right before `put_item`. A float field added later will be converted instead of breaking publishing.\n- **Related problem:** `tags` that aren't a list of strings (e.g. `[1.5]`) caused a 500. They now get a 400.\n\n**Tests:** I added 4 regression tests, including publishing several related stories in a row. All 4 fail on the original code with the same error as production, and all 5 tests pass with the fix.\n\nOne thing I didn't change: `table.scan()` isn't paginated, so it only reads the first 1 MB of the table. Once the library grows, \"similar\" stories will come from only part of it.\n\nThe cause and fix are written up in `ANSWER.md`. Nothing was committed or deployed.","ttft_ms":3052,"type":"result","duration_ms":46262,"uuid":"26bc2c13-47d9-4d86-84f7-819b591ce977","ttft_stream_ms":2465,"time_to_request_ms":34,"first_content_frame_ms":2465,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":12,"outputTokens":3939,"cacheReadInputTokens":136576,"cacheCreationInputTokens":11100,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.1949432,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":581,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}
